    "probe_text": "`POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:113-135`). The V2 controller only adds a paged list endpoint. Here is everything that happens, in execution order. I've tagged each step as a **validation** (can reject the request by throwing) or a **side-effect** (mutates the DTO/owner, derives data, or persists).\n\n## Before anything else\n- **Validation (authorization):** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold the owner-admin role.\n\n## 1. Resolve the registration date \u2014 `effectiveRegistrationDate` (line 116)\n1. **Validation:** if a `registrationDate` was supplied and it is *after* today, throw `InvalidFieldsException(\"registrationDate\")` \u2192 400.\n2. **Side-effect:** pick the supplied date, else today's date.\n3. **Side-effect:** roll it forward to the next business day (Saturday/Sunday \u2192 following Monday; weekday unchanged). This single adjusted date is what everything downstream uses.\n\n## 2. Intake rules \u2014 `prepareNewOwner` (line 117), in this exact order\n4. **Side-effect:** `normalizeAddress` \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand street abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE); null/blank \u2192 empty string. Written back onto the DTO *before* the required-field check, so a blank address is caught next.\n5. **Validation:** `validateRequiredFields` \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank (whitespace counts as blank). Collects *all* offenders and throws `RequiredFieldsMissingException(missing)` \u2192 400 with an `errors` array.\n6. **Side-effect + validation:** `normalizeTelephone` \u2014 strip spaces/dashes/brackets, coerce to E.164 (assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` when no `+`); must match `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, then `validateNationalNumberLength` enforces the per-country national length for recognized codes (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException(\"telephone\")` \u2192 400. Normalized value written back to the DTO.\n7. **Side-effect + validation:** `normalizeEmail` \u2014 optional (null passes through); if present it must match the email pattern and its domain must not be in the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), else `InvalidFieldsException(\"email\")` \u2192 400; the stored value is trimmed + lower-cased. Written back to the DTO.\n8. **Validation:** `validatePostcode(postcode, city)` \u2014 optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region the postcode must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Violation \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException(\"postcode\")` \u2192 400.\n9. **Validation:** `rejectDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, compute the household id from `(lastName, postcode)`; if any existing owner already carries it, throw `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 409. (Owner with no postcode has no household, so never rejected.)\n10. **Validation:** `rejectCityAtCapacity(city)` \u2014 if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive), throw `CityCapacityExceededException` \u2192 409.\n11. **Validation:** `rejectDailyLimitExceeded(registrationDate)` \u2014 if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry this adjusted registration date, throw `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2192 429.\n\n## 3. Build and enrich the owner (lines 119\u2013124)\n12. **Side-effect:** map the (now-normalized) DTO to an `Owner` entity.\n13. **Side-effect:** set `registrationDate` to the adjusted date from step 1\u20133.\n14. **Side-effect:** set `customerCode` = `<REGION|UNKNOWN>-<8 hex of SHA-256(telephone + lastName)>`.\n15. **Side-effect:** set `namesakeCount` = number of *pre-existing* owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive; excludes the new owner).\n16. **Side-effect:** `assignHousehold` \u2014 set `householdId` from `(lastName, postcode)` (null when no postcode).\n17. **Side-effect:** `applyPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 reset `possibleDuplicate=false`/`possibleDuplicateOf=null`; unless `sharesHousehold`, flag it if an existing owner shares `lastName`+`postcode` but has a *different* telephone, recording that owner's id.\n\n## 4. Persist and respond (lines 125\u2013134)\n18. **Side-effect (persistence):** `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 the owner is written to the store.\n19. **Side-effect:** set `householdMemberCount` = owners in the household, counted *after* save (so it includes this owner).\n20. **Side-effect:** emit an `AUDIT` info log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n21. **Side-effect:** map to `OwnerDto` and set `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 owners share this registration date.\n22. **Side-effect:** set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\n### Notes worth flagging\n- The uniqueness/capacity/limit validations (steps 9\u201311) and the derived counts (15, 17, 19) all query `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and run outside any transaction \u2014 `addOwner` is not `@Transactional` (unlike `deleteOwner`), so these check-then-act checks are racy under concurrency.\n- The required-field check (step 5) deliberately runs *after* address normalization but *before* telephone/email normalization, so a whitespace-only address is rejected as \"missing,\" while telephone/email format errors surface as separate `InvalidFieldsException`s rather than \"missing.\""
